WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.020
Sorry, can't stop to talk now. I'm rushed
off my feet with this blooming banquet.

cue-2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.260
Well, this won't be the last barrel of gin
I have to add to the punch. There hasn't

cue-3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:16.059
been a proper election contest here since,
well, before I was born. They usually

cue-4
00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:21.480
just come to an arrangement about which
MPs will represent us. Obvious why. If

cue-5
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:27.120
there's a proper election, all the voters
have to be bribed, and that's expensive.

cue-6
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.659
But that's exactly what's going on here,
an election entertainment. Free drink,

cue-7
00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:38.200
free food for anyone promising to support
the new interest, as they call

cue-8
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.840
themselves.

cue-9
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.930
We had the old interest in here yesterday.
Most people call them the Tories. Look

cue-10
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.580
what they did to the painting of King
William. They really hate 'em.

cue-11
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:56.080
And it's the Whigs in today. Not much to
choose between them, if you ask me. Look

cue-12
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:02.210
around the table, a motley lot. Not all of
'em can vote, of course. I can't for one.

cue-13
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:08.179
But even when I'm older, I won't be rich
enough. Only about one in 20 can vote. No

cue-14
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:13.680
women, nobody under 21, and only those men
who own or rent property of sufficient

cue-15
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:20.020
value. Still, when there's an election,
everyone gets to play a part. If you're

cue-16
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.260
not in here gorging yourself to death,
maybe you're out in the town, marching

cue-17
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.160
through the streets, listening to the
speeches, singing ballads, or picking a

cue-18
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.680
fight. See T. Carter over there with his
bludgeon? Oh, he looks like he's been

cue-19
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.140
doing a good bit of persuading, though
he's taken a few blows himself. Voters or

cue-20
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.920
not, you can't say that these people don't
care about the election. Plus, there's

cue-21
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:50.340
all the money being spent. It's keeping
this inn in business. You should speak to

cue-22
00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:56.070
one of the candidates maybe. You can
hardly notice them in all this commotion.

cue-23
00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:01.780
They're the ones paying for it all. Look,
there they are, behind me, at the end of

cue-24
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.540
the table.
